WEBVTT

00:00:00.162 --> 00:00:05.440
FedRAMP High is an ongoing operational commitment, not a one-time documentation project.

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:09.000
After authorization support work, the system continues to change.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.230
Vulnerabilities are discovered, configurations drift, staff roles change, incidents occur,

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:16.420
dependencies evolve, and new features may alter the boundary.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:19.985
Continuous monitoring is the discipline that keeps security posture visible as the live

00:00:19.985 --> 00:00:21.510
system changes.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:25.360
Continuous monitoring includes vulnerability management, configuration drift detection,

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:28.540
change management, incident reporting expectations at a high level,

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:32.050
periodic evidence updates, risk tracking, plans of action and milestones,

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:35.405
resilience monitoring, privileged activity review, security metrics,

00:00:35.405 --> 00:00:36.880
and operational ownership.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:41.130
The details may evolve, but the principle is durable: risk must be watched, reported,

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:42.280
and managed over time.

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:45.640
High-impact operations require stronger attention to resilience.

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:49.435
Teams should understand backup and recovery expectations, dependency failure modes,

00:00:49.435 --> 00:00:51.630
monitoring coverage, escalation paths,

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:55.280
and how critical services continue or recover during disruption.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:58.010
Resilience does not replace access control, incident response,

00:00:58.010 --> 00:00:59.465
or vulnerability management.

00:00:59.465 --> 00:01:03.045
It complements them by reducing the chance that a failure becomes a severe mission

00:01:03.045 --> 00:01:04.100
disruption.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:06.520
Continuous monitoring also supports federal trust.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:11.035
Authorizing officials and agency customers need confidence that the provider can identify

00:01:11.035 --> 00:01:11.350
problems,

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:14.785
communicate risk, remediate weaknesses, and keep control evidence current.

00:01:14.785 --> 00:01:18.765
A High baseline raises the stakes for that trust because the consequences of failure are

00:01:18.765 --> 00:01:19.800
more serious.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:22.140
The operating model needs to show sustained discipline,

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.000
not a single successful assessment moment.
